From a97a9217e182408a59da097bad5599dc91354780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: common: Let the Headphone Jack control follow
 line out plugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The WCD MBHC reports a plug as SND_JACK_LINEOUT when it classifies it
as high impedance headphones (and when its measurement fails). The
headset jack is created with SND_JACK_LINEOUT in its mask, but only
HEADPHONE and MICROPHONE have pins, so a line out plug changes no
kcontrol and userspace (PulseAudio's JackControl "Headphone Jack")
never learns that something is plugged into the headphone output.

Add SND_JACK_LINEOUT to the Headphone Jack pin: both kinds of plug use
the same output.

Seen on an SM6115 phone (F(x)tec Pro1-X, WCD9370): studio headphones
are reported as line out, the evdev switch shows SW_LINEOUT_INSERT and
both ALSA jack controls stay off.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model traced the jack report path and wrote the change; the author plugged the headphones for every test)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=claude-opus-5-5; retrieval=none
---
 sound/soc/qcom/common.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
index d9f256d51..fa8b372b7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
@@ -334,8 +334,14 @@ static struct snd_soc_jack_pin qcom_headset_jack_pins[] = {
 		.mask = SND_JACK_MICROPHONE,
 	},
 	{
+		/*
+		 * MBHC reports high impedance headphones (and any plug it cannot
+		 * measure) as SND_JACK_LINEOUT. Both use the headphone output, so
+		 * let the Headphone Jack control follow line out plugs too:
+		 * without it such a plug changes no jack control at all.
+		 */
 		.pin = "Headphone Jack",
-		.mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
+		.mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE | SND_JACK_LINEOUT,
 	},
 };
 
